<programme start="20261115150000 +0000" stop="20261115180000 +0000" channel="ACCN ESPN"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Duke at Miami</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 7 Hurricanes (8-1, 6-0 ACC) try to recover as they host the Blue Devils (7-2, 4-2). Miami, which is without star wideout Malachi Toney, lost 31-24 at Notre Dame last week. Duke has won three straight after dismantling NC State, 41-3.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261115180000 +0000" stop="20261115200000 +0000" channel="ACCN ESPN"><title lang="en">Women&apos;s College Volleyball</title><sub-title lang="en">Duke at North Carolina</sub-title><desc lang="en">From Carmichael Arena in Chapel Hill, N.C.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Volleyball</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191298_b_v12_ac.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261115200000 +0000" stop="20261115220000 +0000" channel="ACCN ESPN"><title lang="en">Women&apos;s College Basketball</title><sub-title lang="en">Marshall at Duke</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Marshall Thundering Herd visit the No. 5 Duke Blue Devils for an NCAA Division I game in North Carolina. Marshall features guard Olivia Olson putting up roughly 16.7 points per game, while Duke counters with Arianna Roberson around 12.0 points.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Basketball</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191292_b_v12_bh.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261115220000 +0000" stop="20261116000000 +0000" channel="ACCN ESPN"><title lang="en">Women&apos;s College Basketball</title><sub-title lang="en">Stetson at Clemson</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Clemson Tigers clash with Stetson Hatters in NCAA play. Clemson looks to defend home court behind 11 fast-break points and seven steals from a Nov 12 game, while Stetson relies on seven three-pointers from a six-point road loss to take a win.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Basketball</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191292_b_v12_bh.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261116000000 +0000" stop="20261116020000 +0000" channel="ACCN ESPN"><title lang="en">Women&apos;s College Basketball</title><sub-title lang="en">Canisius at Syracuse</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Canisius Golden Griffins visit the Syracuse Orange. Canisius sits at 2-1 after falling 64-61 to Cornell and relies on Sofia Vitucci who leads in points and assists, while Syracuse seeks its fourth straight victory after beating Siena 82-58.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Basketball</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191292_b_v12_bh.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261116020000 +0000" stop="20261116050000 +0000" channel="ACCN ESPN"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Louisville at North Carolina</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Cardinals (6-3, 5-2 ACC) vie for their fifth straight victory as they visit the Tar Heels (5-4, 2-3). The programs haven&apos;t met since 2017. Louisville quarterback Lincoln Kienholz has accounted for 25 touchdowns this season with 11 on the ground.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261116050000 +0000" stop="20261116080000 +0000" channel="ACCN ESPN"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Syracuse at NC State</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Wolfpack (4-5, 2-4 ACC) and Orange (4-5, 2-5) continue pursuit of bowl eligibility. NC State fell to 1-1 under interim coach Todd Goebbel following a 41-3 setback against Duke. Syracuse has won two straight meetings after a 24-17 verdict in 2024.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261116080000 +0000" stop="20261116110000 +0000" channel="ACCN ESPN"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">California at Virginia</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Cavaliers (4-5, 2-4 ACC) and Golden Bears (3-6, 2-4 ACC) try to snap three-game slides. Virginia won the first meeting, 31-21 in 2025. California, outscored 131-37 in its last three games, faces a sixth losing season in the past seven years.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
